# Inertia Vue Frontend Rules

## Vue And Inertia

- Use `resources/js/pages` for Inertia pages; `app.ts` resolves `./pages/${name}.vue`.
- Prefer `<script setup lang="ts">` for new Vue files.
- Use `MainLayout` for public PetConnect pages; keep existing auth/settings layouts for those sections.
- Reuse `components/ui`, `components/web`, and existing composables before adding new components.
- Use Inertia `<Link>`, `<Form>`, `router`, and `useForm`; do not use Vue Router for page navigation.
- Route helpers are mixed intentionally: auth/settings often use Wayfinder imports, while older domain pages may use Ziggy `route()`. Preserve the file's local style unless intentionally converting it.
- Do not hardcode URLs when a Wayfinder or Ziggy route helper is available.

## Forms

- Use Inertia `<Form>` with Wayfinder `.form()` helpers for simple auth/settings forms.
- Use `useForm` for stateful, multipart, wizard, transform-heavy, or dynamic forms such as pet create/edit, profile edit, comments, reviews, reports, and messaging.
- Keep preview-only fields out of submitted multipart payloads.
- Surface backend validation through existing `InputError` or component-local error UI.

## Shared Props

Shared props come from `HandleInertiaRequests`: `auth.user`, `flash`, `messaging`, `name`, `quote`, and `sidebarOpen`.

Use existing composables when possible: `useAuthUser`, `useFlashToast`, `useAppearance`, `useTwoFactorAuth`, and `useInertiaInfiniteScroll`.

## Styling

- Tailwind is v4 and CSS-first in `resources/css/app.css`.
- Use semantic tokens such as `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-card`, `border-border`, `text-muted-foreground`, and `text-primary`.
- Keep dark mode via `.dark` and `dark:` variants.
- Use lucide-vue-next icons.
- Use shadcn-vue/reka-ui primitives for buttons, inputs, dialogs, sheets, dropdowns, checkboxes, labels, selects, tooltips, cards, alerts, skeletons, and similar UI.
- Prefer gap utilities over sibling margins.

## Verification

- Run `npm run format` for Vue/CSS formatting when needed.
- Run `npx vue-tsc --noEmit` for type-sensitive work.
- Run `npm run build` for route imports, Vite, Tailwind, or broad UI changes.
